1
00:00:00,296 --> 00:00:03,780
Imagine a call arriving at Concrete's Customer Service Center.

2
00:00:04,261 --> 00:00:06,202
The agent answers through Genesys.

3
00:00:06,461 --> 00:00:10,134
but the caller is following up on an exchange request made last week.

4
00:00:10,732 --> 00:00:13,044
The information exists in Zoho Desk.

5
00:00:13,502 --> 00:00:16,199
The challenge is getting it to the right employee.

6
00:00:16,356 --> 00:00:17,407
at the right moment.

7
00:00:18,006 --> 00:00:23,546
Today, as described in Concrete's current workflow, the agent may have to copy the phone number,

8
00:00:23,845 --> 00:00:25,662
Search Zoho Desk manually.

9
00:00:26,061 --> 00:00:30,601
Open the customer's previous tickets and then look for the most recent update.

10
00:00:31,082 --> 00:00:32,382
The search is possible.

11
00:00:32,581 --> 00:00:35,657
but every extra step interrupts the conversation.

12
00:00:36,376 --> 00:00:38,852
Now imagine a more connected experience.

13
00:00:39,371 --> 00:00:41,609
When an inbound call arrives in Genesys,

14
00:00:41,807 --> 00:00:44,690
the caller number starts an authorized customer lookup.

15
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:47,062
if it finds one reliable match,

16
00:00:47,399 --> 00:00:51,872
A screen pop opens the relevant customer context. the contact record,

17
00:00:52,053 --> 00:00:53,371
previous support tickets

18
00:00:53,611 --> 00:00:54,905
their current statuses,

19
00:00:55,103 --> 00:00:56,792
and the latest recorded update.

20
00:00:57,291 --> 00:00:59,349
Let's follow a realistic example.

21
00:00:59,729 --> 00:01:01,911
The customer is asking about an exchange.

22
00:01:02,391 --> 00:01:07,735
The agent can see an earlier ticket and a note saying the request is still pending branch review.

23
00:01:08,134 --> 00:01:09,591
That's a recorded status.

24
00:01:09,890 --> 00:01:11,964
not a promise that the review has happened.

25
00:01:12,503 --> 00:01:15,604
Instead of making the customer explain everything again,

26
00:01:15,822 --> 00:01:18,843
The agent can continue from the last documented point.

27
00:01:19,404 --> 00:01:21,305
If several contacts share a number,

28
00:01:21,443 --> 00:01:25,022
the employee chooses the correct record. If there's no match,

29
00:01:25,303 --> 00:01:27,580
a safe manual search remains available.

30
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,577
and if the lookup service fails,

31
00:01:29,756 --> 00:01:31,730
The call itself must continue.

32
00:01:32,089 --> 00:01:35,010
A phone number alone never proves someone's identity.

33
00:01:35,532 --> 00:01:37,029
Notice what's changing here.

34
00:01:37,409 --> 00:01:40,085
We're not replacing Genesys or Zoho Desk.

35
00:01:40,424 --> 00:01:43,368
and we're not pretending a new integration is already live.

36
00:01:43,867 --> 00:01:48,545
we're proposing a clearer way to connect systems that Concrete already uses.

37
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:51,016
The potential benefit is straightforward.

38
00:01:51,456 --> 00:01:54,231
fewer manual searches, easier follow-up.

39
00:01:54,369 --> 00:01:56,159
and more attention on the customer.

40
00:01:56,596 --> 00:01:59,511
Those benefits must be measured in a real pilot.

41
00:01:59,708 --> 00:02:01,739
not presented as guaranteed savings.

42
00:02:02,258 --> 00:02:06,523
First, we'll review Concrete's existing Genesys pop-up configuration.

43
00:02:06,822 --> 00:02:09,209
Zoho Desk Access, permissions

44
00:02:09,429 --> 00:02:11,441
and the supported integration options.

45
00:02:11,879 --> 00:02:16,419
Then, we'll test the experience with authorized sample calls and validate the results.

46
00:02:16,837 --> 00:02:18,150
The goal is simple.

47
00:02:18,471 --> 00:02:20,052
when the conversation begins,

48
00:02:20,252 --> 00:02:21,928
the context should be ready.

49
00:02:22,326 --> 00:02:27,639
This is the Genesys and Zoho Desk experience proposed by GRINDCTRL for Concrete.
